8. Positioning of MCP and Stateful Agents

Two areas require explicit explanation because they are important and can be misunderstood.

8.1 MCP

MCP is positioned as part of the governed integration layer.

Its role is to provide:
	•	controlled access from AI runtimes to tools and services
	•	consistent handling of context and authorisation
	•	traceability and governed mediation

It should not be interpreted as the integration pattern for all ingestion or enterprise data movement.

8.2 Stateful Agents

Stateful agents are positioned as part of the orchestration and execution model.

They are intended for:
	•	long-running workflows
	•	multi-step reasoning
	•	governed tool usage
	•	scenarios where execution state must persist

They are not assumed to be the default processing path for all content types.

